/E (The history of the CIA triad)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The concept of the CIA Triad is shaped over time and does not have a single creator. "Confidentiality" appeared in 1976 in a study in the U.S. Air Force. The concept of "Integrity" is found in a 1987 dissertation titled "A Comparison of Commercial and Military Computer Security Policies" written by David Clark and David Wilson. The dissertation stated that in commercial data processing, methods are needed to ensure the accuracy of data. As for "Availability", there is no clear initial source, but the concept became well known in 1988, which was also the year when the three components were brought together and formed the concept of the CIA Triad.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
